~ start
Diwa: I can move around with the Arrow Keys (←↑↓→), and interact with objects with the E key.

Diwa: I think I can interact with lots of things, but for now…

Diwa: Maybe I should start by interacting with those pipes over there?

=> END

~ interact_pipe
#(When picking up a pipe)

Diwa: Woof, that’s a bit heavy… 

Diwa: I believe water flows through these pipes though.

Diwa: If I could get the water to flow in from the right direction. Could it bring the water to the flower?

Diwa: Please, hang in there, flower…

=> END

~ interact_hose
#(When interacting with a hose)

Diwa: Hmm… I can turn this handle, but I’m not sure what it does.

Diwa: I did see Gramps send water to these things though. Maybe it does something to the water flow?

=> END

~ interact_sprinkler
#(When interacting with a sprinkler)

Diwa: Oh, I remember playing with these little things! 

Diwa: I think they spray water all over the place. How fun!

Diwa: Though I think I need to supply it with water first.

=> END

~ interact_wheelbarrow
#(When interacting with a wheelbarrow)

Diwa: Woof, this is really heavy… I can push it around to rotate it though, thankfully.

Diwa: I get the feeling this can hold quite a bit of water.

Diwa: If I point it in the right direction, I think this will be useful.

=> END

~ interact_rock
#(When interact with a rock)

Diwa: Arf… It won’t budge!

Diwa: I’ll have to find a way around this rock, somehow.

=> END

~ level1_complete
#(After dawg revitalizes the flower)

Diwa: It… It worked! Phew…

Diwa: I’m glad I was able to save you, pink flower.

Diwa: But… The rest of the garden needs my help, doesn’t it?

Diwa: …

Diwa: I’ll come back soon, flower. I need to go help the other flowers too.

Diwa: Just like Gramps did… I’ll find a way to help everyone. Little by little.
=> END

~ bonus_dialogue
Diwa: Hmm? 

Diwa: …

Diwa: Huh. I didn’t think that would work but, it did. 

Diwa: Well, back to watering the flowers!
=> END
